    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d276-a2">

                <pb facs="0521" n="459" sameAs="frus:frus1944Quebec/pg459"/>

                <head>Appendix “B”</head>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Total Availability of Personnel
                        Shipping by Categories</hi> (as of 1 Oct 1944)</p>
                <table cols="6" rows="8">
                    <row>
                        <cell cols="2"/>
                        <cell cols="2" rendition="#border-bottom"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >British</hi></cell>
                        <cell cols="2" rendition="#border-bottom"><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >U.S.</hi></cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell/>
                        <cell rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#italic">Categories</hi></cell>
                        <cell><hi rendition="#italic">No. of Ships</hi></cell>
                        <cell><hi rendition="#italic">Capacity</hi></cell>
                        <cell><hi rendition="#italic">No. of Ships</hi></cell>
                        <cell><hi rendition="#italic">Capacity</hi></cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell>1.</cell>
                        <cell>Ocean Going</cell>
                        <cell role="num">84</cell>
                        <cell role="num">302,000</cell>
                        <cell role="num">220</cell>
                        <cell role="num">492,000</cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell>2.</cell>
                        <cell>Limited Capability</cell>
                        <cell/>
                        <cell/>
                        <cell/>
                        <cell/>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell/>
                        <cell>(<hi rendition="#italic">a</hi>) Indian Ocean type</cell>
                        <cell role="num">31</cell>
                        <cell role="num">48,000</cell>
                        <cell role="num">—</cell>
                        <cell role="num">—</cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell/>
                        <cell>(<hi rendition="#italic">b</hi>) Miscellaneous</cell>
                        <cell rendition="#underline" role="num">6</cell>
                        <cell rendition="#underline" role="num">6,000</cell>
                        <cell rendition="#underline" role="num">45</cell>
                        <cell rendition="#underline" role="num">35,000</cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell/>
                        <cell rendition="#float-right">Subtotal</cell>
                        <cell rendition="#underline" role="num">37</cell>
                        <cell rendition="#underline" role="num">54,000</cell>
                        <cell rendition="#underline" role="num">45</cell>
                        <cell rendition="#underline" role="num">35,000</cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell/>
                        <cell>Total Troopship Lift</cell>
                        <cell role="num">121</cell>
                        <cell role="num">356,000</cell>
                        <cell role="num">265</cell>
                        <cell role="num">527,000</cell>
                    </row>
                </table>
                <table>
                    <row>
                        <cell><hi rendition="#small-caps">Notes</hi>:</cell>
                        <cell/>
                        <cell/>
                        <cell><hi rendition="#italic">British</hi></cell>
                        <cell/>
                        <cell><hi rendition="#italic">U.S.</hi></cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell cols="3">1. Estimated lift on 1 October 1945, after allowing for
                            additions and losses based on current C.C.S. rates</cell>
                        <cell/>
                        <cell role="num">376,000</cell>
                        <cell/>
                        <cell role="num">708,000</cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell cols="6">2. Additional trooplift may be realized by use of cargo ships
                            temporarily fitted to carry a few hundred troops each.</cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell cols="6">3. An indeterminable lift may be obtained from captured enemy
                            vessels.</cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell cols="6">4. Lift of LSI’s and APA’s is not included in above inventories
                            but advantage will be taken of their lift whenever operational schedules
                            permit.</cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell cols="6">5. Lift in U.S. Navy vessels as estimated and included in the
                            above table for normal troop movement is subject to wide variation
                            dependent upon possible utilization of Navy troopships for operational
                            requirements.</cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell cols="6">6. No British cross-Channel type of shipping is included nor
                            has any allowance been made for possible conversions for the naval fleet
                            train or hospital ships.</cell>
                    </row>
                </table>
            </div>
        </body>
